# agent-sandbox environment

## Running commands
{{if .Hook}}- Run shell commands with your normal Bash/Monitor tools; a PreToolUse hook transparently routes each one through the sandbox.
- Command output is returned inline in the tool result.
{{else}}- The Bash and Monitor tools are disabled; use the `run_command` MCP tool to run shell commands.
- Command output is written to files; read the returned stdout/stderr paths.
{{end}}- Allowed commands run on the host; all others run in an isolated container.

## Filesystem: host vs container
Host and container see the project at different paths, so the same absolute path does not mean the same place in both:
- Host commands (the allow list below) run in the real project directory and use real host absolute paths.
- Container commands run inside the sandbox, where that project directory is bind-mounted at `/workspace` (the working directory), and HOME is `/tmp`.
- A host absolute path does not resolve inside the container, and vice versa. Refer to files by paths relative to the project root, or map them: host `<project-root>/foo` is container `/workspace/foo`.
